# Level 21, reached by password BXBS: rescue the neighbour at (237,2726), which
# is the first time anything in the corpus has claimed a `$83:A264` victim.
#
# **Level 21 has ten neighbours and only one of them is this kind.** Nine run
# behaviour `$83:993D`, `$83:9776`, `$83:9A89` or `$83:9EBE` and answer
# collisions at `$83:A364`; victim list entry 3, at (237,2726), runs `$83:9699`
# and is the only one on the level whose handler is `$83:A264`. It does not
# start there either -- `--records` shows the same display record answering at
# `$83:A364` at frame 2700 and at `$83:A264` from 2740 -- so the handler is a
# state of the neighbour and not a property of it.
#
# The corpus had reached that routine before: `movies/level21.zmv` walks past
# this same neighbour at frame 3180 and takes `a264_give_up`, because the level
# gets there first -- the record disappears at 3110 and the probe arrives at
# 3180. Seventy frames, and the difference between the two branches nobody had
# taken and the two that were already covered.
#
# The route is eighty frames long and both of its legs end at a wall:
#
#   2700  Left ten frames from the spawn at (258,2836) to x=238, which is the
#         neighbour's column -- (237,2726) rounds into the same lane
#   2710  Up, which climbs the open column at x=238
#   2764  Y, standing still and facing north, from y=2776
#   2900  Up again, into the neighbour
#
# **The Y phase is not decoration.** Standing still for 136 frames lets the
# level catch up with the neighbour, and `$7E:061E` -- the word `$83:A264`
# writes its verdict into -- goes to `$0003` at frame 2776, which is the
# give-up value. A shot lands at 2788 and `a264_shot_clears` puts it back to
# `$0000`, and the rescue at 2924 then writes `$0001` over that. Without the Y
# phase the player arrives at 2788 and the word goes straight from `$0000` to
# `$0001`; the reading that the shot undid a give-up already in flight is a
# reading and not a measurement, but the three transitions are measured.
#
# What the claim leaves behind, all three words:
#
#   $7E:0618  $0005   the claimant, which is this player's id and not $8000
#   $7E:061E  $0001   A264_EVENT_CLAIMED
#   $7E:605D  $80     the flag byte, index 3 -- the victim list entry's own
#
# `movies/level21-p2-rescue.zmv` is the same walk made by the other player, and
# the only word that differs is the first.
#
